to the appropriate dispatch method.
.SH CHAN_CONTROL (0) \(en Session lifecycle
CHAN_CONTROL manages the session lifecycle.
It is the only channel that accepts messages before authentication.
.PP
\f[B]Auth flow:\f[R]
.PP
The client sends an \f[CR]auth\f[R] message with the server token.
The server responds with \f[CR]auth_ok\f[R] (success) or
\f[CR]auth_fail\f[R] (failure).
.IP
.EX
Client                          Server
  |                               |
  |  {\(dqch\(dq:0,\(dqtype\(dq:\(dqauth\(dq,       |
  |   \(dqtoken\(dq:\(dqabcdef...\(dq}        |
  |\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\->|
  |                               |
  |  {\(dqch\(dq:0,\(dqtype\(dq:\(dqauth_ok\(dq}    |
  |<\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-|
.EE
.PP
Python:
.IP
.EX
\f[B]await\f[R] client.auth(token)
.EE
.PP
TypeScript:
.IP
.EX
\f[B]await\f[R] client.auth(token);
.EE
.PP
C:
.IP
.EX
int rc = bc_auth(c, token);
.EE
.PP
Java:
.IP
.EX
client.auth(token);
.EE
.PP
\f[B]Ping/pong:\f[R]
.PP
Keepalive mechanism.
The client sends \f[CR]ping\f[R], the server responds with
\f[CR]pong\f[R].
.PP
Python:
