.SH CHAN_COMMAND (1) \(en Command evaluation
CHAN_COMMAND evaluates shell commands and returns the results.
An \f[CR]eval\f[R] request produces a sequence of three response
messages:
.IP
.EX
Client                          Server
  |                               |
  |  {\(dqch\(dq:1,\(dqtype\(dq:\(dqeval\(dq,       |
  |   \(dqcommand\(dq:\(dqecho hello\(dq}     |
  |\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\->|
  |                               |
  |  {\(dqch\(dq:1,\(dqtype\(dq:\(dqstdout\(dq,     |
  |   \(dqdata\(dq:\(dqaGVsbG8K\(dq,          |
  |   \(dqencoding\(dq:\(dqbase64\(dq}        |
  |<\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-|
  |                               |
  |  {\(dqch\(dq:1,\(dqtype\(dq:\(dqstderr\(dq,     |
  |   \(dqdata\(dq:\(dq\(dq,                  |
  |   \(dqencoding\(dq:\(dqbase64\(dq}        |
  |<\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-|
  |                               |
  |  {\(dqch\(dq:1,\(dqtype\(dq:\(dqcomplete\(dq,   |
  |   \(dqexit_code\(dq:0}              |
  |<\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-|
.EE
.PP
The \f[CR]stdout\f[R] and \f[CR]stderr\f[R] payloads are
base64\-encoded.
The client bindings automatically decode them and return an
\f[CR]EvalResult\f[R] object:
.PP
Python:
.IP
.EX
result = \f[B]await\f[R] client.eval(\(dqecho hello\(dq)
\f[I]# result.stdout == \(dqhello\(rsn\(dq\f[R]
\f[I]# result.stderr == \(dq\(dq\f[R]
\f[I]# result.exit_code == 0\f[R]
.EE
.PP
TypeScript:
.IP
.EX
\f[B]const\f[R] result = \f[B]await\f[R] client.eval(\(dqecho hello\(dq);
\f[I]// result.stdout === \(dqhello\(rsn\(dq\f[R]
\f[I]// result.stderr === \(dq\(dq\f[R]
\f[I]// result.exit_code === 0\f[R]
.EE
.PP
C:
.IP
.EX
bc_eval_result_t result;
bc_eval(c, \(dqecho hello\(dq, &result);
\f[I]/* result.stdout_data == \(dqhello\(rsn\(dq */\f[R]
\f[I]/* result.stderr_data == \(dq\(dq */\f[R]
\f[I]/* result.exit_code == 0 */\f[R]
bc_eval_result_free(&result);
.EE
.PP
Java:
.IP
.EX
EvalResult result = client.eval(\(dqecho hello\(dq);
\f[I]// result.stdout == \(dqhello\(rsn\(dq\f[R]
\f[I]// result.stderr == \(dq\(dq\f[R]
\f[I]// result.exitCode == 0\f[R]
.EE
.PP
The \f[CR]eval\f[R] method blocks (or awaits) until all three messages
are received.
The order is always stdout, stderr, complete.
